  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The layering is checkable",
      "items": [
        "core's internal dependency graph is acyclic and four deep; layout, ansi and diff import nothing internal",
        "core has four direct external dependencies: uniseg, go-runewidth, x/sys, x/term",
        "internal/arch fails CI when a boundary is crossed, so the rules are not advice in a document"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Behaviour really is separable",
      "items": [
        "headless owns state, input and semantics, and decides how nothing looks",
        "kit answers what headless refuses: which characters draw a border, which grey is muted text",
        "headless never imports kit, so dropping the appearance layer and keeping the behaviour stays possible"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "One concurrency rule",
      "items": [
        "one goroutine draws and handles input; state reached only from it needs no lock",
        "work that happens elsewhere returns through Runtime.Dispatcher and runs there",
        "the program parks when there is nothing to do — no clock runs regardless"
      ]
    }
  ]
